    "Terrace": "Use case: precise-object-edit / cinematic architectural photography. Edit target: real Old Mike Pub outdoor terrace photograph. User requests premium hyperrealistic cinematic regeneration, NOT the flat portrait snapshot. Create a LANDSCAPE 1536x1024 editorial architectural photograph of this SAME exact recognizable venue. Reframe to emphasize the central terrace and OLD MIKE sign; reduce unnecessary sky and foreground paving; straighten verticals. Preserve original pergola beam layout, corrugated roof, triangular neighboring building, OLD MIKE letters, round window decals, tables, chairs, plants and overall spatial identity. Do not invent a different restaurant, furnishings or crowds. Rich clean late-afternoon light: warm practical string lights, golden wood with believable texture, balanced shadow detail, restrained forest greens, elegant soft side-light, no blown-out sky, no muddy shadows, no orange cast. Make it look like a premium architectural photographer shot the location with excellent lens and exposure. Focus on the real terrace rather than empty sky/floor. Output widescreen landscape with soft natural darkened perimeter for integration into warm charcoal website, but no vignette obscuring architecture. Photorealistic not rendered/painted. No added text/logos, no frame. Keep architectural recognition above stylization.",
    "Covered": "Use case: precise-object-edit, premium hyperrealistic architectural hospitality photography. Source is the ACTUAL COVERED TERRACE of Old Mike Pub. Regenerate a professionally framed cinematic LANDSCAPE 1536x1024 image of THIS location, retaining recognition. Preserve the retractable cream ribbed canopy, black steel structure, full-height glazed wall on RIGHT, dark vertical wood/slat and green panels on LEFT, TV at far end, square wood tables, black-metal wood chairs and green/leaf cushions, grey wood-look floor. Remove the accidental finger at bottom-right. Reframe camera attention at seating eye-level: significantly less empty ceiling and empty foreground floor, tables and perspective main subject. Maintain spatial relationships and architecture; do not turn it into a different luxury interior. Beautiful soft late-afternoon warm sunlight through windows, luminous warm practical light, realistic wood grain, clean rich contrast with details in shadows, subdued olive greens, tasteful amber highlights. No fake people, new furnishings or structural features, no decorative additions. Camera-ready photorealism, not illustration, not a cold phone photo. Wide composition without cropping key architectural landmarks. Soft natural darker edges for warm charcoal site blending, no hard black border, no strong vignette. No text overlay or watermark.",
    "Interior": "Use case: cinematic architectural photograph regeneration of a real restaurant. Edit target is Old Mike Pub INTERIOR seating room. Create a premium hyperrealistic LANDSCAPE 1536x1024 hospitality editorial photo of THIS EXACT recognizable room. Preserve dark structural posts and pitched cream canopy, teal-green banquettes along BOTH walls, square wood tables, olive/mustard/rust upholstered chairs, hanging green foliage and warm pendant bulbs, wood floor and small step/strip light. Camera framing seats and tables, balanced architectural perspective; crop excessive empty ceiling and foreground floor, remove ugly lens flare and haze. Reconstruct clean realistic surfaces while preserving this real layout, no made-up new building or luxury finishes, no people, no new furniture. Cinematic warm interior lighting with softly glowing existing pendants, a little clean window daylight, rich natural olive and amber palette, highly realistic wood and fabric microtextures, good shadow detail, soft rather than blown highlights. Elegant professional interior photography, not orange/black AI look, not illustration. Landscape frame suitable for website with natural soft darker perimeter and no border. Keep clear architectural recognizability.",
